  "title": "Global fashion brands shift orders from Bangladesh to India amid unrest",
  "summary": "Global fashion brands, including Zara and H&M, have diverted nearly a tenth of their monthly orders from Bangladesh to neighboring India, as labor unrest and rising costs have affected production and reduced Bangladesh's competitive edge.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Global fashion brands diverted $254 million worth of orders from Bangladesh between November 1 and 18.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Most orders moved to India, with India being the main destination.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The shift reflects disruptions in production and rising costs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
